  "body": "It appears that currently the only way to close (without aborting) a writable stream is by calling `getWriter`, and then calling `close()` on that writer. Would it make sense to also expose `close()` directly on `WritableStream` itself?\r\n\r\nPresumably you'd only be able to call such a method if the stream isn't locked (just like abort on the stream can only be called if the stream isn't locked).",
